# TruckERP — Rebuild / Restart / npm Commands

**Compose:** Use **`docker compose -f docker-compose.yml`** only (single prod-oriented file).

## API — Full rebuild + restart (most common)

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp

docker compose -f docker-compose.yml build truckerp-api \
  && docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d truckerp-api
```

## API — Restart only (no code change, no rebuild needed)

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml restart truckerp-api
```

## Nginx — Config reload only (`default.conf` is bind-mounted; no image rebuild)

After changing **`infra/nginx/default.conf`** only:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml exec truckerp-nginx nginx -s reload
# or: docker compose -f docker-compose.yml restart truckerp-nginx
```

Do **not** confuse this with **frontend `dist`** updates — those require **rebuilding the `truckerp-nginx` image** (see below).

## Nginx — Full rebuild + recreate (frontend `dist` **or** `infra/nginx/Dockerfile`)

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp

docker compose -f docker-compose.yml build truckerp-nginx \
  && docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d truckerp-nginx
```

## Full stack — rebuild everything and bring up

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp

docker compose -f docker-compose.yml build \
  && docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d
```

## Frontend (npm) — Build for production (output goes to apps/web/dist)

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp/apps/web && npm run build
```

**LOCK:** Prod `docker-compose.yml` bakes `apps/web/dist` into the **nginx image** (`infra/nginx/Dockerfile` `COPY apps/web/dist/`). **`docker compose restart truckerp-nginx` does not pick up new JS** — you must **rebuild the image** after `npm run build`:

```bash
/home/admin/trucking_erp/scripts/reload_nginx_web.sh
```

Or manually:

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml build truckerp-nginx \
  && docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d truckerp-nginx
```

## Frontend (npm) — Install dependencies (after package.json change)

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp/apps/web && npm install
```

## Frontend (npm) — Dev server (local only, not used in Docker)

```bash
cd /home/admin/trucking_erp/apps/web && npm run dev
```

## Check API logs (after restart)

```bash
docker logs truckerp-api --tail 50 -f
```

## Run Alembic migrations (tenant)

**LOCK:** Tenant migrations are authoritative only inside the container. Run from container only (never rely on host venv unless drift is confirmed). Before upgrade, run `alembic -c alembic_tenant.ini heads` in container — must be 1 head. Drift check: `git rev-parse --short HEAD` on host and `docker exec truckerp-api bash -lc 'cd /app && git rev-parse --short HEAD'` in container must match.

```bash
docker exec truckerp-api bash -lc \
  'set -a && . /run/secrets/truckerp.env && set +a && cd /app && alembic -c alembic_tenant.ini upgrade head'
```

## Run Alembic migrations (platform)

```bash
docker exec truckerp-api sh -lc \
  'set -a && . /run/secrets/truckerp.env && set +a && cd /app && alembic -c alembic_platform.ini upgrade head'
```

## API image — psql (postgresql-client) for read-only audit

- **Add postgresql-client in the Dockerfile for truckerp-api** (apt-get install postgresql-client on Debian; apk add postgresql-client on Alpine). Do **not** put it in docker-compose env — env won’t persist the binary and won’t fix “psql not found”.
- **Rebuild the image once** (see “API — Full rebuild + restart” above). After that, any `up -d` or `up -d --force-recreate` keeps psql as long as it uses that image.
- No need to add anything in compose YAML env for this.

One-liner for Cursor: *Install psql in the truckerp-api Dockerfile (postgresql-client / apk add). Once it’s in the image, recreating containers won’t remove it; only rebuilding from a Dockerfile without that line would.*

## When to do what

| Situation | Command |
|---|---|
| Changed Python code (model, router, schema, service) | rebuild + restart API |
| Changed `docker-compose*.yml` or `Dockerfile` | rebuild + restart API |
| Changed frontend `.tsx`/`.ts`/`.css` | `npm run build` → **rebuild** `truckerp-nginx` image → `up -d` (see `scripts/reload_nginx_web.sh`) |
| Changed `infra/nginx/default.conf` | restart nginx only |
| Changed `package.json` dependencies | `npm install` → `npm run build` → rebuild `truckerp-nginx` image |
| Config change (no code change) | restart API only |
| Migration needed | run Alembic (tenant or platform) → restart API |

## IMPORTANT

- NEVER use `docker-compose` (v1 hyphenated). Always `docker compose` (v2 space).
- **Standard deployment:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.yml` (single file).
- Working directory for all Docker commands: `/home/admin/trucking_erp`
- Frontend build output: `apps/web/dist` (served by nginx as static files)
